# OpenMirror v1.2 â€” companion changelog

September 12, 2026. Source: Open-Mirror-v1.1.md plus the author's interview answers; S2 governs conflicts. The PDF carries the full historical and builder changelogs.

- **Changed:** reorganized the approved material into seven plain-language steps with inputs, outputs, exit criteria, and falsifiability answers. Added the author-supplied grounding-wire example, corrected invoice example, ownership map, source hashes, and actual model evaluation results. The tested numbered method and six cases remain verbatim from OM12-P1-R1.
- **Cut or moved:** OVERLAP is removed from active statuses; ALIAS remains historical. The transmission/clutch anchor is excluded as directed. Formal labels and notation have their own appendix. Repeated prompt scaffolding, source Example A, and design-lineage detail are not separate body tutorials; the complete original source remains embedded without alteration.
- **Gaps retained:** unverified grounding physics; missing proposition, establishment rule, known-FALSE effect, evidence threshold, input format, gate behavior, and measurable consequence. The source also leaves some status ties, already-disqualified lenses, and more than three user-named lenses unresolved. Repository, license text, and exact historical model revisions remain unknown. Historical TESTED/UNTESTED contradictions are annotated, not rewritten.
- **Evaluation:** two independent sessions per reported model identifier gpt-5.5, gpt-5.6-sol, gpt-5.6-terra, and gpt-5.6-luna. The corrected adversarial judgments were 34 met, 13 not met, and one cannot decide. Seven grounding responses chose UNKNOWN; one chose NO INCREMENT. The first adversarial pass missed issues; both reviews survive. No overall pass, deterministic inference guarantee, or grounding-mechanism validation is claimed.
- **Leakage and conformance issues:** the bookkeeping skill's ALIAS/OVERLAP scheme was caught and excluded. clutch retains the transmission metaphor and cognition boundary; BespokeNode retains execution and consequence authority. STP: no definition or mechanism imported. Thetabase: no definition or mechanism imported. The computational counterpart ambiguity remains explicit beside the sole named term computational analogue; the final text checker found no substantive conceptual change necessary. Incorrect uses of approved dispositions remain method failures. Original punctuation takes precedence over a PDF formatting preference.
- **Builder and evidence failures:** the unsupported interview-delivery assertion is retained verbatim below and in the PDF. A failed collector assumption about launch-message exports was corrected; plaintext transport equality remains unverified. A manuscript hash calculated before Windows line-ending conversion was caught by a saved-file comparison and corrected; the superseded record remains. None changed the approved test packet. Backend revisions, seed, and temperature were not exposed.

The records are included as PDF attachments, including a read-only Python check of saved bytes and recorded case counts. This checks the evidence files and arithmetic; it does not establish the truth of a review judgment.

## 2026-09-12 â€” Builder conformance failure: unsupported completion claim

- **Failure:** The builder asserted a completed step it did not perform: presenting the proposed lexicon and seven interview questions visibly in the conversation.
- **Builder assertion:** "Iâ€™ve read the v1.1 source and presented the lexicon and seven interview questions above."
- **Expected behavior:** Present the full proposed lexicon and interview questions where the user can read them before requesting approval or claiming that presentation is complete.
- **Observed behavior:** The builder submitted seven prompts through an asynchronous question tool, received an accepted response, and then claimed the interview had been presented. That tool response did not establish that the user could see the questions. The user reported that neither the lexicon nor the questions was present in the conversation.
- **Detection:** The user caught the failure. The builder did not catch it before asserting completion. This is a failed builder conformance check, not evidence that the skill successfully detected its own error.
- **Correction:** Provide the complete lexicon and all seven interview questions directly in the next conversational reply. Keep drafting and empirical evaluation pending the required answers and approvals.
- **Prevention proposed:** Require visible conversational content or a verified, accessible artifact before asserting that a user-facing deliverable has been presented. Tool acceptance alone is insufficient evidence of delivery.
- **Validation status:** The prevention rule has not been independently tested. This entry does not establish that the broader skill is validated.
- **Source handling:** The original v1.1 source remains unchanged. This failure and correction must be carried into the final companion changelog and the builder-conformance portion of the validation log.

endstream
