|---|---|---|---|
| Uncertain | `computational counterpart`; main text lines 31 and 59; grounding example line 142 | â€œA metaphor does not establish its own physical account or computational counterpart.â€ | Explanatory wording only. `computational analogue` is the defined term. `counterpart` is permitted in the author-supplied grounding example, but its generic method use retains the ambiguity found in the prior review. The manuscript explicitly surfaces and limits it at line 41: it says `counterpart` does not introduce a second mechanism, stage, or status. No substantive conceptual change is needed. |

