OpenMirror v1.2 â€” accompanying records

Save all PDF attachments into one folder. To verify the stored records and recalculate
the case counts, run: python verify-records.py
The verifier uses only Python's standard library, reads local records, and prints a
result. It does not make network/model calls or execute the grounding-wire proposal.

The packet, original sources, cases, raw final responses, and review files retain
their original bytes. response-model-key.json reveals the IDs after anonymous review.
The reviewed-packet manifest retains its preparation-time status; subsequent owner
approval is in pre-dispatch-hash-verification.json. The local launch-message file is
not included because it contains a workstation path; its original hash remains in
the reviewed manifest. Exact common instructions and case inputs are included in
replicator-packet.txt. This is a portable evidence subset, not a claim that every
local execution log is attached. The public run metadata is an explicitly selected
extract. The launch transport's plaintext could not be independently checked from
local exports. Backend revisions, temperature and seed were not exposed.

The publication manifest hashes every other attachment. Its own digest is outside
that list to avoid self-reference. A manifest verifies correspondence to recorded
hashes; it does not authenticate the author or make the file tamper-proof.
Original reviews and their corrections both remain. Calculation conformance does
not establish semantic correctness or a successfully validated physical mechanism.

endstream
