# Source-fidelity review by the builder

Date: 2026-09-12. Builder runtime identifier: gpt-6-astra; reported effort: ultra. This review is separate from the anonymous model replications and adversarial review.

The original source and author amendments were retained byte-for-byte. The frozen candidate, vocabulary, source text, instructions, and cases matched the owner-reviewed manifest before dispatch and during subsequent checks. This establishes file identity, not semantic truth.

## Method trace

| Candidate section | Governing source | Finding |
|---|---|---|
| Purpose and responsibility | S1 introduction/operating rules; S2 sections 1 and 4 | Exploratory scope and execution handoff preserved. |
| Crosswalk and twingineering | S2 sections 1 and 4; original task's falsifiability rule | Definitions and three questions are explicit; no mechanism test is asserted. |
| Steps 1-5 | S1 numbered workflow and output pattern; S2 section 5(a) | Baseline, lens limit, break point, and literal return precede grading. |
| Step 6 | S1 firing tests; S2 section 6 | Four active statuses; OVERLAP removed; NO INCREMENT first and RELATED last. |
| Step 7 | S1 disposition; S2 section 1; approved P1 gap handling | NO INCREMENT excluded from disposition; held candidates retain explicit missing falsifiability fields. |
| Grounding example limits | S2 section 3; approved P1 gap handling | Physical account and computational gate remain untested and incompletely specified. |
| Invoice corrections | S2 section 5(b-c) | Organizational question is out of scope; ecology's discarded result is a disposition. |
| Boundary map | S2 sections 1, 3, and 4 | Meaning/cognition/consequence ownership preserved; no sibling mechanisms imported. |
| Failure modes | S1 rules; S2 section 4; original task; authorized builder-failure record | Both recurrence warnings and the builder's failed completion claim remain distinguishable. |
| Notation appendix | S1 labels and count; S2 example states and boundaries | Symbols are crosswalked to plain language; unspecified truth conditions are not invented. |

## Limits and disagreements

- The lexicon checker marked generic use of computational counterpart as uncertain because computational analogue is the defined method term. The phrase occurs in S2's example and in the exact candidate the owner reviewed. The publication must state explicitly that computational analogue is the sole named method term; counterpart is descriptive wording, not a second mechanism or stage. The checker's uncertainty is retained, not silently erased.
- The candidate and final publication are source-derived specifications, not proof that a model will follow them. The anonymous responses contain rule-use failures, documented by the original adversarial review and its preserved addendum.
- The builder challenged the first adversarial pass using exact response quotes and existing P1 criteria. The reviewer revised eight rows, preserving one unresolved judgment. This is evidence that the first reviewer pass missed issues, not evidence of an infallible review process.
- Known gaps remain: the grounding proposition and gate semantics; a complete tie rule for supported statuses; an active status for every already-disqualified lens; and handling more than three user-named lenses. The approved gap handling exposes these rather than inventing rules.
- No substantive material from earlier GPU work, sibling project files, external browsing, or the bookkeeping skill supplies the OpenMirror method. The bookkeeping skill's ALIAS/OVERLAP scheme was rejected as a vocabulary conflict.
- The PDF skill's preference for ASCII hyphens does not override the owner's requirement to retain source history and the builder-failure entry verbatim. Original punctuation is preserved in those passages.

## Execution-record limits

The recorded replicator tool calls are local reads or hashes of the frozen packet. There is no recorded mechanism execution, external evidence lookup, or peer-response access in those calls. Requests to read a complete file and later chunks do not prove the model understood all of it.

Runtime metadata reports the requested model identifiers and medium reasoning effort for all eight sessions. Exact backend revisions, temperature, and seed are not exposed. Fresh sessions omit parent conversation history but still receive platform context and instructions. Shared provider/model ancestry and writing-style clues limit claims of independence.

The reviewed launch message was supplied in the conversational dispatch calls. Local parent exports represent that message as an opaque transformed value, and child user-message exports do not contain its plaintext. A failed collector assumption about where to find the launch was corrected in metadata version 2. The initial metadata was retained. No plaintext transport-equality claim is based on those opaque exports, and no protected content was decoded.

This record is not a final PDF visual or textual conformance check. That check follows document assembly.

endstream
